{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 53, :comments ["<b>And the Levites shall camp around.</b> The verse explained above why they shall camp around: so that no one from the congregation of Israel will approach the Tabernacle and die. And this is the meaning of \"and there will be no wrath\" — like Uzzah, who touched the Ark, and there it is written, \"And the anger of YHWH burned against Uzzah.\"" "And the meaning of <b>over the congregation of Israel.</b> [is] one of their congregation. And similarly, \"and he was buried in the cities of Gilead\" [meaning] the city of the son of the donkeys, and many like these." "<b>And the Levites shall keep.</b> A commandment upon them to guard the Tabernacle."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:57.186578793Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}